{"version":1,"herramienta":"whisperx medium + wav2vec2 es (letras)","audio":"ovario.m4a","duracion":36.544,"texto":"El ovario humano está formado por una medulla interna y una corteza externa, cuyos límites no son claramente distinguibles. La medulla contiene bases sanguíneos y nervios mientras que la corteza alberga folículos en diferentes etapas de desarrollo. En la imagen también se observa un cuerpo lúdico, estructura que se forma tras la ovulación. Los folículos que no liberan su avosito sufren un proceso denominado degeneración, denominado traición folicular. convirtiéndose en folículos atrésicos. El cuerpo lúctio puede mantenerse funcional gracias a la acción de la hormona luteinizante y la gonadotropina coriónica humana.","cues":[[0.0,"X"],[1.513,"H"],[1.613,"E"],[1.733,"A"],[1.873,"D"],[1.973,"C"],[2.114,"E"],[2.274,"X"],[2.534,"F"],[2.634,"A"],[2.694,"B"],[2.774,"E"],[2.834,"B"],[2.954,"D"],[3.054,"E"],[3.134,"B"],[3.194,"D"],[3.294,"E"],[3.495,"B"],[3.715,"D"],[3.855,"C"],[4.015,"H"],[4.175,"D"],[4.355,"B"],[4.595,"D"],[4.675,"F"],[4.795,"D"],[4.936,"E"],[5.016,"B"],[5.136,"C"],[5.196,"B"],[5.256,"D"],[5.376,"C"],[5.436,"B"],[5.656,"D"],[5.836,"F"],[5.916,"C"],[5.976,"B"],[6.096,"C"],[6.417,"B"],[6.537,"E"],[6.697,"B"],[6.817,"D"],[6.897,"B"],[6.957,"D"],[7.017,"C"],[7.077,"B"],[7.157,"C"],[7.377,"B"],[7.638,"A"],[7.758,"C"],[7.838,"B"],[7.938,"X"],[8.298,"D"],[8.418,"C"],[8.578,"F"],[8.638,"H"],[8.698,"D"],[8.798,"E"],[8.878,"B"],[8.978,"C"],[9.039,"B"],[9.099,"C"],[9.159,"D"],[9.259,"B"],[9.539,"C"],[9.639,"E"],[9.719,"C"],[9.879,"B"],[10.059,"C"],[10.119,"B"],[10.239,"C"],[10.319,"B"],[10.58,"C"],[10.68,"D"],[10.8,"E"],[10.86,"B"],[11.0,"C"],[11.08,"B"],[11.14,"D"],[11.24,"H"],[11.38,"C"],[11.46,"B"],[11.6,"D"],[11.66,"E"],[11.901,"C"],[12.041,"F"],[12.141,"E"],[12.221,"B"],[12.441,"G"],[12.521,"C"],[12.641,"B"],[12.861,"C"],[12.961,"D"],[13.061,"B"],[13.262,"C"],[13.422,"D"],[13.502,"B"],[13.622,"H"],[13.722,"E"],[13.822,"X"],[14.322,"B"],[14.382,"D"]